1. The outset of your ttyrec has you trying to eat a tengu when there
are elf corpses right there.  Moreover, it was a peaceful tengu in
sokoban.  Leave it alone until later; sleep res is nearly as high-
priority as poison res.
2. Pets can help tremendously when you're asleep.  Leaving sokoban, a
dog came running up to you practically begging to be tamed and you
killed it.  There were several other domestic monsters along the way,
too.
3. You were carrying around unID'd tins.  I always eat right away
(assuming satiation isn't an issue) to see if they might have good
intrinsics.  They're not good emergency rations anyway, may as well
see what they are.

Early on like this, I'll let domestic pets eat chameleon corpses if
possible, there are plenty more around to tame if I wind up with a pet
yellow light.

2 other questions:
1. Where were your missile weapons?  A hail of daggers is a mighty
tool.
2. I wouldn't bother advancing hammer to skilled unless you think it
really enhances short-term survivability (e.g. if you're struggling to
hit things), long-term you're going to want to go with Excalibur.


